libmount: add missing fileutils.h include to hook_idmap.c

util-linux 2.42.3 backported the openat2() hardening for CVE-2026-78410,
which makes hook_idmap.c use RESOLVE_NO_SYMLINKS, but it did not backport
the follow-up that adds the include providing the fallback #define for
that constant. The fallback lives in include/fileutils.h, and
hook_idmap.c does not include it, so the build fails with

  libmount/src/hook_idmap.c: In function 'hook_mount_post':
  libmount/src/hook_idmap.c:335:33: error: 'RESOLVE_NO_SYMLINKS' undeclared

glibc 2.40+ masks this because its <bits/fcntl-linux.h> transitively
includes <linux/openat2.h>. musl does not, so hadron hits it on both
amd64 and arm64.

Fixed upstream by 7e2e01087 ("libmount: add missing fileutils.h include
to hook_idmap.c"), which is on master but not in the 2.42 stable branch.
Drop this patch once a 2.42.x release carries it.

--- a/libmount/src/hook_idmap.c
+++ b/libmount/src/hook_idmap.c
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 
 #include "strutils.h"
 #include "all-io.h"
+#include "fileutils.h"
 #include "namespace.h"
 
 #include "mountP.h"
